<title>LEBANON: Chirac tells Brittan to mind his own business.</title>
<headline>Chirac tells Brittan to mind his own business.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac hit back at European Trade Commissioner Leon Brittan on Friday for criticising his drive for a European role in Middle East peace efforts.</p>
<p>Asked at a news conference for his comment on Brittan's statement that individual European countries should abstain from any independent action, Chirac said:</p>
<p>&quot;That the commissioners should abstain from all interference in matters that are not theirs.&quot;</p>
</text>
